<http://data.silknow.org/object/80a9b859-15b7-3b4e-a7fd-8940a6abe8ba>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk and cotton on a linen ground, described upon acquisition as \"looped weaving.\" The pattern consists of 23 narrow vertical stripes containing repeating patterns of birds, lozenges, and chevron ornaments. There is a border all round of conventional human figures and dentations, with a short looped fringe in mauve and white silk. The colours are chiefly red, green, nad buff (in silk) and blue (in cotton)."@en , "Woven silk cotton linen with birds and human figures; Italy; 1700s."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/7e03cce5-202c-36fb-a61c-801a8ced39c9> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Woven silk cotton linen with birds and human figures; Italy; 1700s."@en , "Silk and cotton on a linen ground, described upon acquisition as \"looped weaving.\" The pattern consists of 23 narrow vertical stripes containing repeating patterns of birds, lozenges, and chevron ornaments. There is a border all round of conventional human figures and dentations, with a short looped fringe in mauve and white silk. The colours are chiefly red, green, nad buff (in silk) and blue (in cotton)."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/80a9b859-15b7-3b4e-a7fd-8940a6abe8ba/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/80a9b859-15b7-3b4e-a7fd-8940a6abe8ba/dimension/1> ;
